# Who must review a change before it can merge.
#
# The main ruleset requires CODE-OWNER review and no other approval, so the file below IS the
# review policy: a PR that touches only unowned paths merges without anyone looking at it, and a
# PR that touches anything owned waits for the owner. The last matching line wins.
#
# THE STAGING LANE. web/internal/staging/ is deliberately left unowned so a teammate can add a
# page of their own, and the Staging index lists it by itself (scripts/_staging_index.py). The
# PR check "Staging lane" (scripts/_staging_lane.py) is what keeps that safe, and it is required
# on main. It also fails when a folder under staging/ is neither a lane page nor listed here, so
# a legacy page cannot quietly fall out of ownership.
#
# THE LEGACY PAGES below stay the owner's. A page joins the lane by being new, or by carrying a
# staging.json on main. Do not add a lane page to this list: that would put it back in the queue.

